      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "An airplane flies over the Pacific Ocean at $850$ meters above sea level. At the same time, a submarine is in the ocean at $125$ meters below sea level. What is the difference in the altitude of the submarine compared to the airplane?",
      "worked_solution": "To determine how far below the submarine is compared to the airplane, we must calculate the difference between the location of the submarine and the location of the plane. This gives\n\n$$\n850-(-125)=850+125=975.\n$$\n\nThus, the submarine is $975\\,\\text{m}$ below the airplane.",
